"comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/c8utsx/react_angular_di"},{"short_id":"lektbl","created_at":"2015-01-03T10:03:15.000-06:00","title":"Innovation - What Every Developer Absolutely Needs to Know","url":"http://vimeo.com/44723521","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003e\"How to achieve real innovation and market success is often non-intuitve, especially for the typical technically-focused and logically-minded developer driven to make programs run faster, make code more beautiful, add cool features, or use the latest hot technology. Writing great code isn't nearly enough; if developers want their systems to succeed, then regardless of whether they work on proprietary systems or open source, they need to fully understand how innovation and markets actually work. In this talk, Steve will explain critical aspects and details of innovation, based in part on example projects and products from his 28 year career. \"\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"\"How to achieve real innovation and market success is often non-intuitve, especially for the typical technically-focused and logically-minded developer driven to make programs run faster, make code more beautiful, add cool features, or use the latest hot technology. Writing great code isn't nearly enough; if developers want their systems to succeed, then regardless of whether they work on proprietary systems or open source, they need to fully understand how innovation and markets actually work. In this talk, Steve will explain critical aspects and details of innovation, based in part on example projects and products from his 28 year career. \"","submitter_user":"SeanTAllen","user_is_author":false,"tags":["philosophy","practices","video"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lektbl","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lektbl/innovation_what_every_developer"},{"short_id":"akqj4m","created_at":"2015-01-03T07:48:19.000-06:00","title":"Stop Misquoting Donald Knuth!","url":"http://www.joshbarczak.com/bl